<title>THAILAND: Thai mutual funds take money out of finance firms.</title>
<headline>Thai mutual funds take money out of finance firms.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai investment mutual funds have taken defensive moves by withdrawing funds deposited in finance companies amid market concern over the stability of cash-strapped finance firms, banking sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>They told Reuters that Thai investment funds had gradually redeemed funds they kept in promissory notes issued by finance firms in recent weeks.</p>
<p>Cash withdrawals increased after the Bank of Thailand instructed 16 finance companies to suspend business for one month and to produce merger plans within a fortnight, they said.</p>
</text>
